   "id": "scm_call1_evening_clear",
   "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, mp=6 ra_lw=1 ra_sw=1 sf_sfclay=1 sf_surface=1 bl_pbl=1, radt = 30 min) dumped by the instrumented fork ctessum-claude/WRF (module_esm_dump hooks inside SUBROUTINE RRTM after GASABS and inside RTRN of phys/module_ra_rrtm.F; dump scm_ref2_1.json). RRTM has no standalone real64 driver, so every expected value is the real32 in-model value and the tolerance contract is rel 1e-5. Inputs are the dumped extended-column state (TAVEL, TZ, PZ, CLDFRAC, TAUCLOUD, SEMISS, TBOUND) and the GASABS outputs PFRAC and ITR (140 g-points x 103 layers, injected as flattened columns); the gas optics themselves are not transcribed. Expected values: the RTRN fluxes TOTUFLUX/TOTDFLUX and clear-sky TOTUCLFL/TOTDCLFL at every RRTM level, the per-band fluxes at the surface, model top and top of the column, the Planck integrals PLANKBND/PLVL/PLAY, and the heating rates HTR/HTRC (K/day). The scheme is diagnostic (no time step). Regime: call 1, 19:00 UTC (12:34 LST), first radiation call; clear sky (no cloudy layer); tbound = 288.00 K, glw = 258.1 W/m^2, olr (model top) = 251.5 W/m^2, TOA upward flux 244.8 W/m^2. Tolerances: measured against a NumPy replica of RTRN the component's fluxes agree with the real32 dump to <= 1e-6 relative (2e-4 W/m^2), the band fluxes to 2e-5 W/m^2, the Planck integrals to 2e-10, and the heating rates to 4e-4 K/day (HTR is a difference of O(300 W/m^2) fluxes over O(6 hPa) layers carried in single precision, so its relative error is ~1e-4 of the column maximum); tolerances are set 3-5x above those floors: fluxes rel 1e-5 spot / Linf abs 1e-3 W/m^2, band fluxes Linf abs 1e-4, Planck Linf abs 1e-9, HTR/HTRC Linf abs 2e-3 K/day and spot checks rel 1e-4 at the three largest-|HTR| layers.",
   "inputs": "scm_ref2_1.json",
   "reference": "scm_ref2_1.json",
   "column": 0,
   "time_span": {
    "start": 0,
    "end": 1
   },
   "tolerance": {
    "rel": 1e-05
   },
